- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The user-sources facts of `SourceLibraryTests` become a contract suite that any user-sources store runs (001 §C 'Contract tests'; .spec-md §9; the S2.3 brief's 'proxy part of SourceLibraryTests'), as step 66 did for materials. This step moves facts and adds no store. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs`: the helper `userSource` takes `(id : ElementValueId)` in place of a `string`, so a fixture holds its id elevated where it is born (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'): each caller passes a text id as `ElementValueId "<text>"` and a minted one as `newSourceId ()` itself. `[<AbstractClass>] type SourceProxyContract ()` declares `abstract freshSources : unit -> SourceProxy`, a user-sources store holding no user source. These two facts become `[<Fact>]` members of the contract: `the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes`; `the user-sources store refuses a blank name, a non-positive wavelength, and a protected source`. `the user-sources store inserts, replaces by id, and removes` saves its source under `newSourceId ()` where it used the text id `src-user-1`, because the database keys every entry by a GUID (001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'; step 20); its assertions are unchanged. `type SourceLibraryTests () = inherit SourceProxyContract ()` is the in-memory store: `freshSources` is `SourceProxy.createInMemory ()`. The other facts stay members of `SourceLibraryTests` alone: `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal`; `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`; `the live Library offers and resolves a user source after the seeded ones`; `the live Library resolves a sample created in the samples store`; `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`; `the seeded sources are protected, uniquely identified, and cover the lasers and the lithography lines`; `the seeded tree lists every seeded source under Sources`. The private helpers (`nm`, `userSource`, `sourceIds`) move unchanged into a private module above the classes. (2) The in-memory class keeps the name `SourceLibraryTests`, so every fact keeps its id. The abstract contract gets no `ADD_TEST`, and the file keeps its compile position.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `SourceProxyContract` MUST be an abstract class holding the two user-sources store facts and `SourceLibraryTests` its in-memory subclass, and `SourceLibraryTests.fs` MUST NOT contain `src-user-1`; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with its count unchanged and every SourceLibraryTests fact under its old id; and build, elevation and the eleven s10 invariants MUST pass.
